        "datePublic": "2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z",
        "title": "FreeRDP 2.0.0 before 3.32.0 Heap Buffer Overflow via MP3 Audio Decoding",
        "descriptions": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "value": "FreeRDP 2.0.0 before 3.32.0, when built with WITH_LAME=ON and WITH_DSP_FFMPEG=OFF, has a heap-based buffer overflow in freerdp_dsp_decode_mp3 because the right-channel PCM pointer is offset by a byte count treated as short elements. A malicious RDP server can send MP3 audio over rdpsnd so decoded samples cross the heap allocation, crashing the client."
          }
        ],
        "problemTypes": [
          {
            "descriptions": [
              {
                "lang": "en",
                "description": "Heap-based Buffer Overflow",
                "cweId": "CWE-122",
                "type": "CWE"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
